              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sueb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed the recipe so that I could enjoy this! I used plain yogurt instead of vanilla, and soy milk instead of whole milk. I used equal amounts of ground coconut and water instead of cream of coconut. Then, I forgot to add the ice cubes! This turned into a smooth, rich smoothie! Wonderful recipe, even with my adaptations!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TommyMommy2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this using coconut milk instead of whole cows milk, due to milk allergies. Really good. Tried it again the next day, but only had chocolate yogurt. It was just as good. Fruits or veggies could easily be incorporated to change up the taste as desired. It was very thick, even without the coconut cream. The cream really makes the smoothie sweet and thick.",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-25T11:06:50.670Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Yoly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought this was pretty good. I added a bit more cream of coconut to sweetened it up a little more. I sipped half of it and made popsicles with the other half. I liked the popsicles better.",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-27T21:10:01.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Summer W"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very interesting combination! Seems kinda incongruous, though - LOW-FAT yogurt with avocado, whole milk &amp; coconut cream?? Why not Happy Fats all the way? I tried it with my own whole milk yogurt (with vanilla and a touch of honey added) along with the rest of the good stuff, and omg, it was sooo creamy and delicious! Beats ice cream by a mile if you ask me! Thanks for the recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-11T19:01:49.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MellowHypeINSA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great smoothie, I love avocados and coconut so as soon I saw this recipe I had to try it. only changes I made where instead of using vanilla yogurt I used coconut yogurt and added a hint of tequila, turned out amazing.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-20T02:33:56.653Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Seattle2Sydney"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Can't give an accurate review since I did change it. However, the end result was great! I didn't have any vanilla yogurt so I used the natural/plain yogurt I had on hand. I added some vanilla, honey and a banana to sweeten it. Everyone loved it, even the avocado-hating kid who actually saw the avocado go in and was brave enough to try it!",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-09T21:57:36.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Julie Julie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made mine dairy-free by using all coconut milk instead of yogurt/milk/coconut cream. I added a frozen banana for extra creamy flavor. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-04T12:08:53.110Z"
          },
          {
